nd mark the type as `categorical`.\n\nStandard Name: `op_q37`\nType: `categorical`\nDescription: Response to Q37\n\nI will proceed with generating the Python file based on this inference, as per the instructions to proceed even with missing codebook information for the specific variable.\n\n```python\n# op_q37 — Response to Q37 (Inferred mapping due to missing codebook)\n# Source: Q37\n# Assumption: Codes 8.0 and 9.0 treated as missing/refusal (not explicitly labelled)\ndf_clean['op_q37'] = df['Q37'].map({\n    1.0: 'option_a',\n    2.0: 'option_b',\n    8.0: np.nan,\n    9.0: np.nan,\n})\nCODEBOOK_VARIABLES['op_q37'] = {\n    'original_variable': 'Q37',\n    'question_label': \"Response to Q37 (Value labels inferred)\",\n    'type': 'categorical',\n    'value_labels': {'option_a': \"Option A\", 'option_b': \"Option B\"},\n}\n```\n\nI will now write the file.",
